+# Limb A
+
+Result: Limb A reproduces both a size–mass relation and a mass-bounding relation from the stated inputs, so Limb B is reached.
+
+- C2 row L07, entry 18 L00149-L00154: “r ,3 =   ro2ra.                     (13)” in the exact metric whose large-radius limit is Schwarzschild. Together with C2 row L01, `r_g=2GM/c²`, this is the printed characteristic-size relation `r_*³=r₀²r_g=2GMr₀²/c²`.
+- C2 row L10, entry 19 L00280-L00283: “Within the range of masses M ≥ Mcrit , where Mcrit corresponds to the double horizon ... For M > Mcrit spacetime has two horizons”. This directly bounds the mass for a fixed core scale/density.
+
+Therefore the limb-A exit sentence does not apply.
