+# C2 completion ledger
+
+The four complete numbered-text, disposition, reconciliation, equation-list, and eleven-term-search artefacts are `C2_census_entry18.txt`, `C2_census_entry19.txt`, `C2_census_entry20.txt`, and `C2_census_entry55.txt`. Reconciliations are 286=286, 937=937, 753=753, and 1196=1196 non-blank lines/dispositions, respectively (3172=3172 in the bytes actually read).
+
+| id | candidate premise or relation considered | status | pinned source, locator, verbatim support / named assumption |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| L01 | Exterior gravitational radius and mass identity | SOURCE_DERIVED | `../bhu-reading-20260823/sources/dymnikova_1992_grg24_235_vor_clean.txt`, L00095-L00098: “where” / “2GM” / “rg=       c~'                       (6)” / “and M is the mass of a source measured by a distant observer.” The extraction's `c~` is the printed denominator `c²` as also fixed by the displayed Schwarzschild metric context. |
+| L02 | Mass kind is distant-observer/Schwarzschild (ADM-asymptotic) mass | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 18, L00098-L00100: “and M is the mass of a source measured by a distant observer. The Schwarzschild geometry describes the gravitational field of a spherical mass in e m p t y space outside the mass.” |
+| L03 | De Sitter core scale-density relation | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 18, L00126-L00129: “where r0 is connected with e0 by the de Sitter relation” / “3c 4” / “r~-    87CGeo'                       (9)” (printed extraction of `r₀²=3c⁴/(8πGε₀)`). |
+| L04 | Enclosed mass definition | SOURCE_DERIVED | `../bhu-reading-20260823/sources/dymnikova_2019_universe_clean.txt`, L00222-L00230: “The mass function M(r ) reads:” / “M(r ) = 4π” / “Zr” / “ρ( x ) x2 dx.” / “(3)” / “0”. |
+| L05 | Total mass and asymptotic radius | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 19, L00234-L00245: “A density profile ρ(r ) should provide the proper asymptotic behavior of R g (r ), including vanishing as r → ∞ quick enough to guarantee finiteness of the total mass.” / “M = 4π” / “Z∞” / “ρ( x ) x2 dx < ∞; R g (r → ∞) = r g ; R g (r → 0) =” / “0” / “r3”. |
+| L06 | Exact density profile, coupling mass and core scale | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 19, L00254-L00256: “where ρ0 is the vacuum density at r = 0. In [14], the exact analytic solution has been found for the density profile ρ(r ) = ρ0 exp (−r3 /r02 r g ), representing vacuum polarization in a spherical gravitational field estimated in the frame of a simple semiclassical model [17,24].” |
+| L07 | Equivalent characteristic-size relation | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 18, L00149-L00154: “Ra(r)=r a 1 - e x p ... (12)” / “and” / “r ,3 =   ro2ra.                     (13)” / “This is the exact spherically symmetric solution of the Einstein equations which for r >> r, practically coincides with the Schwarzschild solution and for r << r, behaves like the de Sitter solution.” |
+| L08 | Metric and horizon equation | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 19, L00200-L00220: “The metric ... belongs to the Kerr–Schild class ... and can be written as” followed by `ds²=(1−R_g(r)/r)dt²−dr²/(1−R_g(r)/r)−r²dΩ²; R_g(r)=2GM(r)` and “(2)”. Hence horizons are roots of `g_tt=1−R_g(r)/r=0`. |
+| L09 | Regularity and de Sitter limit | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 18, L00152-L00154: “This is the exact spherically symmetric solution of the Einstein equations which for r >> r, practically coincides with the Schwarzschild solution and for r << r, behaves like the de Sitter solution.” Entry 18 L00205-L00206: “(limr_.o(Rg(r)/r) = 0) that is regular both at r+ and r_ as well as at r -* 0”. |
+| L10 | Black-hole mass bound and critical surface | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 19, L00280-L00283: “Within the range of masses M ≥ Mcrit , where Mcrit corresponds to the double horizon, the de Sitter–Schwarzschild geometry (2) describes a regular black hole with the de Sitter interior [14,24], called a Λ black hole (ΛBH) in [26]. For M > Mcrit spacetime has two horizons, an event horizon r = r+ and an internal Cauchy horizon r = r− .” |
+| L11 | Core density is a free source parameter, not a measured constant fixed by the manifest | SOURCE_DERIVED | entry 19, L00254-L00255: “where ρ0 is the vacuum density at r = 0. In [14], the exact analytic solution has been found for the density profile ρ(r ) = ρ0 exp (−r3 /r02 r g )”. The passage defines ρ₀ but supplies no equality fixing its value; the exhaustive census contains no later fixing relation. |
+| L12 | Euclidean-volume completion kind | SOURCE_DERIVED | BOUND by L04: the printed `4π∫ρ(x)x²dx` already fixes the spherical volume measure; no completion instantiated. |
+| L13 | Uniform-interior completion kind | SOURCE_DERIVED | BOUND by L06: the printed exponential profile fixes a nonuniform interior; adding uniformity would contradict it, so no completion instantiated. |
+| L14 | Order-unity-coefficient completion kind | SOURCE_DERIVED | BOUND by L01, L03-L08: the operative metric, mass integral, exponential argument, and core relation print their coefficients; no unbound order-unity coefficient occurs in the derived family, so no completion instantiated. |
+| L15 | GR-exterior completion kind | SOURCE_DERIVED | BOUND by entry 18 L00140-L00154: the whole mass is connected by the Schwarzschild relation (6), and the exact metric “for r >> r, practically coincides with the Schwarzschild solution”; no completion instantiated. |
+| L16 | Entry 20 candidate Bardeen/type-1 inequality | SOURCE_DERIVED | `../bhu-reading-20260823/sources/gr-qc_0611022_clean.txt`, L00143-L00149: “Type 1 traces back to Bardeen’s work ...” and `A(ρ)=1−Mρ²/(ρ²+q²)^(3/2)`; “two horizons exist provided q²<(16/27)M².” This is a separately parameterized Bardeen example, not the Dymnikova exponential metric used for the study question; retained in the census, not used in the derivation. |
+| L17 | Entry 55 interior-only horizon caveat | SOURCE_DERIVED | `../bhu-reading-20260823/sources/2007.06664_clean.txt`, L00671: “Here we are assuming that a black hole event horizon exists. Note that any analysis that is purely based on the interior geometry does not imply the existence of the event horizon.” This is the loop-quantum interior branch, not the Dymnikova exponential metric; retained in the census, not used in the derivation. |
+
+No candidate row is `UNRESOLVED`. No `ADDED_COMPLETION` was used. The absence of a printed numerical fixation of ρ₀ is demonstrated by the exhaustive per-line census and is reported as surviving freedom, not as an unresolved source proposition.
+
+C2_COMPLETION_LEDGER=PASS
